  "notes": "Distinctive: a study viewer that overlays colour-coded pill chips straight onto PDF text, each colour standing for a visualization type (pink = 3D Model, lavender = Formula, blue = Graph, green = Source, amber = Animation). Selected chips get a dark outline and a hover tooltip like 'Graph: Carrier saturation'. Clicking a chip renders that concept in the right Visualizer panel (checked live: a 3D WebGL membrane model with a 'DRAG · SCROLL' hint). The panel header's Visualizer dropdown switches the panel between study modes (Knowledge Graph, Chat, Flashcards, Quizzes, Feynman), each with a one-line description, and the overflow menu offers 'Regenerate visualization'. The warm off-white (#f6f5f2) canvas shows behind white rounded panels; floating white pill toolbars for page and zoom controls sit at the bottom of the reader. In the tall capture the chip overlays are misplaced; the chip bboxes quoted use the indexed element coordinates."
